   {
    "id": "i2",
    "kind": "Javadoc",
    "lines": [
     17,
     32
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Sample pairs of (PaxDate, equivalent ISO LocalDate) used to verify round-trip conversion. <p>The Pax calendar epoch is 0001-01-01 (Pax) == 0000-12-31 (ISO). Each row is {@code {paxDate, isoDate}} where converting the ISO date via {@code PaxChronology.INSTANCE.date(isoDate)} must yield the given Pax date. <p>Cases are grouped by theme: <ul> <li>Early CE dates near the epoch</li> <li>Leap-year boundaries (year 6 has a 14th \"Pax\" month)</li> <li>Century boundaries (year 399/400/401)</li> <li>Historical dates (1582, 1945, 2012)</li> <li>BCE (negative proleptic year) dates including leap-year boundaries</li> </ul>"
   },
